---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: The timers of a card and the page
  accDescr: Home Assistant hands a card new states. A card on the page starts what it needs, such as the countdown of a tournament, the time a summary shows, idle mode and the history stream. A card that left the page starts nothing. Leaving the page stops every timer and the stream; when the card comes back, it is updated and starts them again. In npm test, the cards of a test leave the page when it ends; a timer that still runs then fails the test with its name and what the timer calls, and stops.

  STATES["Home Assistant hands<br/>the card new states"] --> ON{{"Is the card<br/>on the page?"}}
  ON -- "yes" --> START["It starts what it needs:<br/>countdown, summary time,<br/>idle mode, history stream"]
  ON -- "no" --> NOTHING["It starts nothing"]
  START --> LEAVE["The card leaves the page:<br/>every timer and the stream stop"]
  LEAVE --> BACK["Back on the page, the card<br/>is updated and starts them again"]
  NOTHING --> BACK
  LEAVE --> CHECK{{"npm test: a timer still running<br/>when a test ends and its cards left?"}}
  CHECK -- "no" --> PASS["The next test starts<br/>without its cards and timers"]
  CHECK -- "yes" --> FAIL["The test fails with its name and<br/>what the timer calls; the timer stops"]

  classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef failed fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
  class ON,START,LEAVE,BACK,CHECK bot
  class NOTHING,PASS done
  class FAIL failed
